WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.390
Last time on...

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.060
<i>Love Live! Sunshine!!</i>

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.400
The desire to enter the next Love Live
revitalized the members of Aqours.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.650
But then, we got the news.

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:11.400
To tell you the truth,
the school open house...

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.070
...will be canceled.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.120
The news hit us really hard,
and we thought it was hopeless, but then...

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:19.870
Let's make a miracle happen!

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.200
Let's struggle as hard as we can!

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:28.670
Let's give it all we've got!
Let's shine together until the very end!

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.540
I'm sure things will work out okay, right?

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:44.100
But it's still true that the number
of prospective students hasn't increased.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:47.460
If there aren't students,
the school can't go on.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.000
Mari-<i>san</i>.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:54.070
"Director's Office"

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.090
How did it go?

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:56.700
I'm sorry, but he said that no matter
how many people are opposed to it,

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.240
a school can't survive without students.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.580
I guess that's just expected.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:04.960
So I asked him if he'd reconsider
if we have more prospective students.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:05.790
What?

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:09.790
I asked him how many students
we'd need to recruit

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:11.750
in order to keep the school alive.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:12.630
And?

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:15.130
A hundred.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.710
A hundred...

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:17.670
Right.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.250
He said if we had at least

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.350
a hundred prospective students by the end of the year,

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.600
they'd recruit for the next school year
and hold an entrance exam.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.190
A hundred? We only have ten as of now.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.040
And we have to have a hundred
by the end of the year?

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.050
But at least there's a chance now.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.190
It's not over yet.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.660
It doesn't matter whether
it's possible or not right now.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.160
Because we just have to do it!

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.670
Well, I guess she's got a point.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.790
Mari-<i>chan</i>! Thank you!

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:50.920
Chika-<i>chi</i>!

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:55.420
As long as there's a chance, let's have faith!

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:59.130
Let's try hard for the school
open house and Love Live,

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.800
and find a hundred students!

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:03.260
From zero to one...!

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.890
From one to ten...!

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:06.070
And from ten...

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:07.990
to a hundred!

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:24.160
<i>Let's throw our all at each other</i>
<i>and grab hold of the future!</i>

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:34.800
<i>The sky and this ocean are both on our side</i>

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.760
<i>Shining and saying, "Go, do your best!"</i>

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:45.470
<i>To let our voices reach far, far away</i>

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:50.390
<i>Shall we shout our dreams louder?</i>

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.150
<i>(Full of hope)</i>

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:56.480
<i>Today pulls tomorrow toward itself</i>

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:05.080
<i>It's really fun to grasp the magnet</i>
<i>in my heart and run right now!</i>

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.200
<i>(Let's always go together)</i>

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.000
<i>What shall we do about the future?!</i>

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:17.800
<i>Everyone laughs and cries</i>
<i>as</i> <i>they</i> <i>look for the shape of their dreams</i>

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:26.220
<i>Because I'm sure the</i> <i>future</i> <i>us</i>
<i>will have the answer</i>

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:34.310
<i>Let's run with everything we have</i>
<i>and become the shining wind</i>

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:37.650
<i>We got dream</i>

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:43.610
Ahhhh... I know I said that, but...

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:45.120
"#2 'The Sound of Rain'"

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.120
Already?

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:51.080
I didn't expect that the Love Live qualifiers
would be held this soon.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.460
Yeah, there are many groups entering it, so...

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.540
Our district's qualifiers
will be held early next month.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.340
A special stage will be set up for it.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.630
Evil spirits congregate
to partake in an epic festivity!

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.180
But why is it a problem if it's held sooner?

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.220
That's because... uhm...

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.600
Probably because she has to write lyrics.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:09.430
Oh, I see.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:12.730
Ahhh! This isn't fair!
It's not just me, you know!

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:16.360
Riko-<i>chan</i> complained that
composing two songs is a lot of work, too!

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.690
On that note, You-<i>chan</i> complained, too.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.280
Yeah, I have to do it for nine people, so...

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.650
Can't we use songs we already performed?

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.070
Unfortunately, Love Live rules require us

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:29.410
to perform songs we've
never performed anywhere else.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.250
Love Live is pretty tough.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.000
Those who overcome that hardship

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.000
are the only ones who can
see the view from the summit.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.620
I know, but...

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:46.550
So, are you making
any progress with the lyrics?

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:51.180
Aah! Y-Yeah, I know I need to hurry up, so...

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.060
"Lyrics Notebook"
"Don't Peek!!"
"Chika"

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.060
I found her lyrics notebook here, <i>zura</i>.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.520
Aaaaaaaaah!

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:03.990
"Lyrics Notebook"
"Don't Peek!!"
"Chika"

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:00.730
This is amazing, <i>zura</i>!

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.320
This looks exactly like her.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.990
That's pretty good, isn't it?

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:07.490
I stayed up until 2 a.m. last night and--

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:08.590
Ah...

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.470
Chika-<i>chan</i>...

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:12.790
Yeah...

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:21.250
But I feel bad having Chika and Riko-<i>chan</i>
do all the song stuff like this.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:24.470
Then Kanan, would you like to create
lyrics for the first time in a long while?

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:27.220
N-No, I don't think I can.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.970
You used to do that.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:32.350
By that argument,
you used to compose, too, Mari.

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:33.890
Then who did the costumes?

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.620
Well, that was me, and...

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:41.230
Oh, yeah. Ruby-<i>chan</i>'s good at sewing.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.690
It's not really like that...

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:46.150
This, too! Ruby-<i>chan</i> made it for me, <i>zura</i>!

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:47.320
That's cute!

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.230
Did you do the embroidery, too, Ruby-<i>chan</i>?

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:50.190
Yes.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.650
Then why don't we try splitting up the work?

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.040
Splitting up the work?

00:05:56.210 --> 00:06:01.590
You, Chika-<i>chi</i>, and Riko will create a song
to perform at the open house,

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.090
and the other six
will create a song for Love Live.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.880
If we do that,
everyone's burden will be reduced.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:11.930
But creating a song for Love Live?
I don't have any experience.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:14.260
That's why we'll work on it together.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.480
We've sung on stage before.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:18.980
We might be able to create
a better song than Chika-<i>chi</i>'s group.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:24.440
Not "might be able to." We must,
since we're their <i>sempai</i> as school idols.

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.150
That's the spirit!

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:27.290
That's a good idea!

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:30.240
Then, we'll compete to see
which group creates a better song!

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.180
Ruby-<i>chan</i>!

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.220
Y-Yep.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:32.990
Understood.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:37.450
Well, sounds like we all agree
that we'll create songs in groups.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:40.280
Okay! Let's work hard together!

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:44.760
Well, then, we'll go to Chika-<i>chan</i>'s house
and work on a song there!

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:46.670
Good luck, <i>zura</i>!

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.680
Did you ask your sisters to put
Shiitake-<i>chan</i> on a leash? You did, right?

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:51.040
--So... where should we work?

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.090
Don't worry. Shiitake won't bite.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:53.350
Don't worry. Shiitake won't bite.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:54.260
If we want to stick around here,
maybe at the club room?

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:56.560
Like I told you before, that's not the point.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:56.430
Don't you think we should
try someplace else for a change?

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:58.180
Good point.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:01.850
Maybe we'll do like Chika-<i>san</i>'s
group and pick someone's house?

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:03.150
What about your place, Mari?

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.400
What? My place?

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:09.070
It is true that her house
has large rooms and is close by.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:12.610
Could it be that
Mari-<i>chan</i>'s family is super rich?

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.160
Yep, it seems that way.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:17.490
The secret lair of one
who sits atop the school caste...

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:18.290
--Gulp.
--Gulp.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:22.460
It's no problem for me,
but is it okay for the three of you?

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.250
--Woosh!
--I'm all for it, <i>zura</i>!

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:25.460
Same here!

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:26.880
You have my word as Yohane!

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.420
Okay! Let's go together!

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:33.930
Wow...!

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.640
This is so beautiful!

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:37.970
Something about it feels so cozy, <i>zura</i>!

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:40.400
I feel my inner darkness being sapped away...

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.520
Really?

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.690
When we came here for the first time,
you too were like...

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:48.000
I'm gonna live here!

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.290
Was I?

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:53.570
Anyway, we came here
to create a song. Now, let's start.

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:55.660
Wow...

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:59.410
Thanks for waiting! It's time for afternoon tea.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.000
It's the future big time, <i>zura</i>.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.540
Have as much as you like.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.000
Oh, wow...!

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.370
These macarons are cute!

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:10.010
My cheeks are melting, <i>zura</i>...

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.470
You mustn't, Yohane!

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:15.260
If you get mesmerized
by things like this, you'll be purified!

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.800
Purified, I say!

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.060
Your pitch-black pride
as a fallen angel will be...!

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.360
Open wide...

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:22.600
Shock...!

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.020
And now, I ascend...

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.520
What was that about?

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.060
Dia and Kanan, have some, too.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:37.120
"Chocolate Flavor"

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.530
I'm so happy, <i>zura</i>.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:34.490
This chocolate flavored one
is totally irresistible.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.950
I can't stop eating it, <i>zura</i>.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:40.410
By the way...
what did we come here for again?

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.520
Ah! It's an elephant!

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:51.170
Ahem! As I thought, we can't
get any work done at Mari-<i>san'</i>s place!

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.140
It's hopeless!

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.130
Awww...

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.760
I like the other place better, <i>zura</i>.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.760
I wanted to eat more popcorn!

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.560
Time to work.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:08:59.510
--Yes, ma'am.
--Yes, ma'am.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.470
First, we'll think about
the concept of the lyrics.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:05.140
What do we need in order to
pass the qualifiers for Love Live?

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.100
Yep! That'd definitely be...

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.190
"Nothingness"

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:08.550
...nothingness, <i>zura</i>.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:10.680
Nothingness?

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:11.910
That's right, <i>zura</i>!

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:23.950
"Nothingness"

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:15.320
That is to say, nothingness
doesn't mean there's nothing,

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:18.030
but it means the state
of nothingness exists, <i>zura</i>.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:19.620
That is, indeed, nothingness.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:20.290
Huh?

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:21.170
What?

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:23.000
What the heck is that...?

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.160
That's cool!

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:28.920
Yoshiko-<i>san</i>, the state of
pure nothingness is indeed

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:33.050
the ultimate mental state
that we can reach, <i>zura</i>!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:37.680
Yohane... Nothingness...
That is, complete darkness...

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.600
And the power that comes from it...

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:42.720
--Clank!
--That's right, <i>zura</i>!

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.480
You two are amazing!

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:46.940
Can we really win in Love Like with that?

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:48.940
The theme is too difficult.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:52.440
Of course! I think a happier theme is better.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:53.110
What?!

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:56.530
--To think that they don't get it...
--It's unfortunate for them, <i>zura</i>.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:59.620
So, Mari-<i>san</i>, do you have an idea then?

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.620
Leave it to me!

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:07.950
I've got a super novel happy song
that I've long been nursing!

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:12.290
This feeling that I get
when people listen to my songs...

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:14.460
It's been two years since the last time!

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:15.880
It's the future, <i>zura</i>.

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:16.950
What's the song like?

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.430
Would you like to hear it?

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.480
"Do Not Remove"
"Shiitake"

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.440
"Tochiman Inn"

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.400
Yay!

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.940
Let's mosh! Let's headbang!

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.940
This is kinda good. It sort of
makes you want to move your body.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.860
Let's mosh! Let's headbang!

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.860
Well, it's true that this is a genre
that we've never tried before.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:44.200
If you move your body to the music,
you'll feel happy!

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:48.370
Yeah, this is for Love Live.
We should show energy!

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:51.710
I don't do well with this kind of music.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.590
I hear a high-pitched ringing.

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:56.630
It's just loud noise... Flop.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:10:59.760
Nothing seems to come to mind?

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:04.430
Hmm... I do think that
"shine" is the key word, but...

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.930
"Shine," huh?

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:10.860
Yeah. We'd better hurry up or
Kanan-<i>chan</i>'s group will beat us, right?

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.190
"Ruby Kurosawa"
"New messages: 1"
"Read them now" "Cancel"

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:14.190
Ruby-<i>chan</i>?

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:18.240
She wants us to come right away.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.660
No way! They really beat us?!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:25.280
We can't win in Love Live
with a song like that!

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.220
Don't tell me... you already finished it?!

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:30.910
Are you saying that if we
go with <i>that</i> song we can win?!

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:33.380
It's better than Hanamaru's lyrics!

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:36.920
But I feel that that song
isn't suited for Aqours.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:41.180
Challenging new things
can open up a new future!

00:11:41.180 --> 00:11:42.760
And then, add some koto to it!

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.970
And the state of nothingness, <i>zura</i>!

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.800
There's no way we'd reach that state!

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:50.890
<i>Love Live! Sunshine!!</i>

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:51.940
"Love Live! Sunshine!!"

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:57.770
Maybe we can't
create songs together after all.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:11:59.840
Humph!

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:01.530
Our tastes are too different...

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:03.280
I see...

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:06.370
I thought it was a good idea.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.870
Why don't you talk it over more?

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.290
We did talk it over quite a bit.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:14.500
"Kurosawa"

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:14.500
But the differences in what we like
are bigger than I thought, so...

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:17.000
Totally different, huh?

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:21.970
It's true that the third-year students and
the first-year students are quite different.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:26.550
But if we use that as an excuse,
we won't be able to come together.

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:28.140
That's...

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.350
You are right.

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:36.110
Our communication may be critically lacking.

00:12:36.110 --> 00:12:40.860
The first-years and the third-years
haven't been talking much, so...

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:45.740
Yoshiko-<i>chan</i> and Hanamaru-<i>chan</i>
tend to keep to themselves.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:50.660
It may not look it, but Mari-<i>chan</i>
and Kanan-<i>chan</i> are kind of shy, too.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.060
Then...

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:55.330
Getting to know each other?

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:58.210
That's right. We'll start from there.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:01.010
Trusting each other is important
for creating a song.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.400
But what do we do, <i>zura</i>?

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:05.430
Leave it to me.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:06.970
You've got an idea?

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:12.350
Yep! If you want to become friends
with someone you don't know...

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.350
...you play together! That never fails!

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:18.360
Nice ball!

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:20.440
What's this...?

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:21.480
<i>Zura</i>...

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.240
Now, here it comes!

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.900
Mari's Shining...

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:26.720
<i>Zura</i>!

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:27.780
Leave it to me!

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:29.950
Darkness consumes power.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.660
By extinguishing the light,
its power is neutralized

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.790
and dragged down into the depths
of darkness. That is, indeed...

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:38.710
...Tornado!

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:41.460
Dark Space-Time Consumption!

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:44.690
<i>Zura</i>?!

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:46.470
Ruby!

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:49.430
Are you okay?! Hang in there!

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:49.430
Oh?

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.350
"<i>Tsugaru</i> by Osamu Dazai"

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:54.310
This place is most comfortable
for me after all, <i>zura</i>.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:55.890
Yeah.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:00.640
My heart that was defiled by the light
is now being purified by darkness!

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:03.400
That face!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:06.280
What's your problem?
It's stigma! Stigma, I say!

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:12.240
"Seas around the World"

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:08.660
I'm bored.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:12.240
Yeah, me too. Let's go to the sea. Sea!

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:16.080
Of course, reading is fun even when
you're doing it by yourself, <i>zura</i>.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:19.460
But if we read together, we can tell
each other what we thought of the book,

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.040
Are they sleeping?

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.040
so we'll be able to get to know each other
and it's more fun that way, <i>zura</i>.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:24.090
"Seas around the World"

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:25.210
Their attention spans are pretty short.

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:25.210
so we'll be able to get to know each other
and it's more fun that way, <i>zura</i>.

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:28.930
So... this is something I sort of figured out.

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.180
There are two groups.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:34.010
Wow... Today is a perfect day for diving!

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:36.270
Let's do it together again.

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:39.060
The third-year students,
who like outdoor activities...

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:40.200
Whoa!

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:43.570
I shall summon my new little demons here.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:47.490
...and the first-year students,
who like indoor activities.

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:49.110
What should we do?

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:50.990
I guess we have no choice.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:53.240
--What?
--You know what to do, <i>zura</i>?

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:56.100
At a time like this, we just need to...

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:58.540
...reveal who we are!

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:00.210
In other words,

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:02.170
we need to completely open up to each other.

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:04.460
--Open up?
--How simplistic, <i>zura</i>.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.350
Silence. Since olden times, in Japan,

00:15:07.350 --> 00:15:09.170
bathing together has been part of our culture.

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:14.000
It helps us to better communicate
and work together.

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.720
But taking a bath this early?

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:20.730
There's no way that a fallen angel
would reveal her body!

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:21.970
Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>!

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:26.230
They've got a milk bath of darkness, <i>zura</i>!

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:30.570
--Black or white, make up your mind!
--Grin.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:35.910
This... This pathos is spreading
throughout my body!

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:38.870
You look creepy bathing with
that grin on your face, <i>zura</i>.

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:39.660
Shut up!

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.000
I'm bored of this now.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.090
Yeah. I've been in here long enough.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:47.670
Geez... Have a little patience!

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.670
Huh? Where's Ruby-<i>chan</i>?

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:54.910
This is heavenly!

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:04.150
We just took a bath, and now it's raining...

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:05.730
Here, Kanan.

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:07.900
Thanks.

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.030
I don't know if we achieved anything at all.

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:13.160
Yeah. I wonder what we went there for.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.990
I'm pretty satisfied, <i>zura</i>.

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:16.160
Me, too.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:20.540
I can't make one side happy without
letting down the other. Seriously...

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:23.170
We might have just made
our differences more obvious.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.000
What do I do? I didn't bring my umbrella.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:29.800
What're we going to do? Should we
go back to where we were earlier?

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:31.510
I'd rather not.

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:34.880
Ah-choo! We might've made
no progress after all.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:44.190
There is a temple that my family
is acquainted with nearby, <i>zura</i>. But...

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:45.250
What?

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:51.690
You can come in, <i>zura</i>.

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:52.440
What...?

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.090
I-Is this the place?

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:54.950
Is it really okay?

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:58.120
When I contacted them,
they said we could use this place freely.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:01.870
Where's the owner of this temple?

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:04.870
He doesn't live here...

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:08.170
...so he isn't here, <i>zura</i>.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:12.260
I guess we have no choice
but take shelter from the rain here.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:15.380
Yeah, it doesn't look like the rain
is going to stop any time soon.

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:22.180
The power of darkness... The power
of little demons... I feel their pres--

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:23.640
This is a place of Buddhism, <i>zura</i>.

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:24.760
I know!

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.610
Hey, where's the light switch?

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:30.690
They have no lights, <i>zura</i>.

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:31.770
Really?!

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:41.850
Wh-Wh-What do we do? I'm f-fine, but...

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:43.580
Hug!

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:47.250
There's nothing to do here...
so why don't we work on a song?

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:50.340
But won't you guys fight again?

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:55.670
W-Well, we're gonna need a song,
so why don't we just give it our best shot?

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.260
Yeah.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.260
--Hug!
--Oh, gee... Kanan-<i>san</i>.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.260
Who knows? Maybe we'll be able to create one in a flash.

00:18:00.260 --> 00:18:01.680
That would be nice, <i>zura</i>.

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.680
How are you guys coming with the lyrics?

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:07.310
I saw Yoshiko-<i>chan</i>
writing some the other day, <i>zura</i>.

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:08.850
Don't peep on me!

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:10.480
Hey, good job.

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:12.100
--That's wonderful!
--Great!

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:15.900
All right, my little demons.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:20.570
But can you find... the great Yohane's ark?!

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:22.230
I found it, <i>zura</i>!

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:23.160
Hey!

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:24.290
This is...

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.790
Th-The Ordeal of Shooting Scars?

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:28.290
The Order of Shooting Stars!

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:31.840
What're these spots marked in black?

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:33.100
They are Black Blanks.

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:34.300
I can't read them.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:38.090
Humph! Obviously that's how
it appears to you. Obviously!

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:40.780
If it can't be read by anyone,
it's meaningless, <i>zura</i>.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:43.390
So, how is the composing coming?

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:44.350
It's coming along.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:47.270
I'm sure Chika-<i>chi</i> and the others
like energetic music, too!

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:49.440
--Oh, so it was you.
--But that one is...

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:50.770
It's just not my thing, <i>zura</i>.

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:54.530
Hold on. This Black Blank thing moves.

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:57.220
S-Sis, that's a bug!

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:00.360
Huh?

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:01.270
<i>Zura</i>?

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:17.580
What on Earth is going to happen to us?

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:20.920
We can't work together at all, <i>zura</i>.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:25.310
We'll never be able to create a song like this.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.390
Yeah...

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:29.990
So... bad...

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:34.210
Are we so different?

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:42.570
The roof is leaking, <i>zura</i>.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:43.780
What're we going to do?

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:45.740
I found some plates here.

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:48.620
It's leaking here this time! Let's see...

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:52.210
Mari-<i>san</i>! I found a couple of bowls here.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:54.340
Can I have a plate here, too?!

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:55.160
Okay!

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.630
I want one, too, <i>zura</i>.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:58.210
Sis! Find a bucket! A bucket!

00:19:58.210 --> 00:19:59.210
Ah, Ruby.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:57.520
The tempo, the tone, and the volume...

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:01.280
They're all different from each other
and out of sync, but...

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:03.780
They're coming together one by one.

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:06.280
They're harmonized one by one.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.030
And they're becoming a song.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:11.180
So are we, <i>zura</i>.

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:23.130
Okay! We'll have a training camp
here tonight, <i>zura</i>!

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.740
--What?!
--<i>Zura</i>?!

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:31.170
Chika-<i>chan</i>!

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:33.770
What're you doing there?

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:37.560
Shining.

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:38.320
What?

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:40.320
I saw something.

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:44.140
What I want to say now... What I'm thinking...

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:48.010
The answer to the question
that I was asking myself...

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:49.850
Chika-<i>chan</i>...

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:52.580
Chika!

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:56.530
Ah! Everyone!

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:59.210
Did you finish the song?

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:01.170
We did!

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:02.420
"Composition Notebook!!"
"Aim to pass the qualifiers!!"
"Don't fall asleep!!" "Wake up!!"

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:02.420
Ta-da!

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:03.960
Really?!

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:07.470
"Tochiman Inn"

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:06.470
Now we have to practice!

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:09.150
Since we've got two songs,
we have to try harder!

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:10.360
Yep!

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:13.480
For our school, and for Love Live!

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:14.980
"Incoming Call"

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:18.100
<i>Try and be brave</i>

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:20.650
<i>I know it's actually scary</i>

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:26.650
<i>It's not like I was able</i>
<i>to</i> <i>do it from the start, either</i>

00:22:26.650 --> 00:22:29.490
<i>I messed up a lot</i>

00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:32.160
<i>I was really frustrated</i>

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:37.710
<i>But</i> <i>that</i> <i>gave</i> <i>me</i> <i>strength,</i>
<i>so</i> <i>just</i> <i>don't</i> <i>give</i> <i>up</i>

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:43.420
<i>Tears</i> <i>in</i> <i>your</i> <i>eyes</i>
<i>that</i> <i>want</i> <i>to</i> <i>try</i> <i>believing</i>

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:47.680
<i>Say "bye-bye" to hesitation and tears</i>

00:22:47.680 --> 00:22:49.340
<i>Now, let's go!</i>

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:54.520
<i>Let's chase them as</i> <i>many</i> <i>times</i>
<i>as it takes, don't lose</i>

00:22:54.520 --> 00:22:57.770
<i>Everyone fails sometimes</i>

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:00.810
<i>But dreams won't fade, dreams won't fade</i>

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:06.190
<i>Let's chase them as</i> <i>many</i> <i>times</i>
<i>as it takes, don't lose</i>

00:23:06.190 --> 00:23:14.240
<i>'Cause today is today, and once</i>
<i>you</i> <i>wake up, it'll be a new morning</i>

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:22.250
<i>Oh, the sun's smiling down on you</i>

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:41.450
"#3 'Rainbow'"

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:38.860
Next Time! "Rainbow."
